# dotenvx + Bitwarden (local env)

Canonical how-to: [`docs/dotenvx.md`](docs/dotenvx.md). Stack: [dotenvx](https://dotenvx.com/) · [Bitwarden custody](https://dotenvx.com/docs/custody/bitwarden/).

## Model

| Place | Format | Private key |
|---|---|---|
| Dev PC (Win/macOS) | Encrypted `.env` (`encrypted:…`) | Bitwarden (`dotenvx bitwarden up`) — not git |
| VPS `/opt/twitch-telegram-bot` | **Plaintext** `.env` (compose / deploy scripts) | N/A |
| Public git | `.env.example` only | Never `.env.keys` / `DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY` / `BW_SESSION` |

Do **not** commit production ciphertext to the public GitHub remote. Sync encrypted `.env` between personal machines privately (or Bitwarden note); second PC is set up separately.

## Agent must

- Load via `dotenv_loader` / `config.py` — never invent a second parser
- Prefer `dotenvx set KEY "value"` for encrypted local updates (then sync VPS plaintext per [`twitch-client-secret.mdc`](twitch-client-secret.mdc))
- Run local bot with `dotenvx run -- python main.py` (or after Bitwarden unlock / `.env.keys`)
- Keep `.env.keys`, plaintext secrets, Hostkey/API keys, `BW_SESSION` out of chat, commits, logs — print counts/prefixes only
- Refuse committing `.env.keys`; remind `dotenvx bitwarden up` if a private key appears on disk after encrypt
- Docker image: no `.env` / `.env.keys` (`.dockerignore`)

## Agent must not

- Put private key or vault session in source / README / rules examples with real values
- Replace VPS plaintext workflow with encrypted-only without an explicit user request
- Log decrypted env or `bw` / Hostkey tokens
- Assume Bitwarden custody is done while `.env.keys` still holds `DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY=…`

## Quick commands

```bash
dotenvx encrypt
$env:BW_SESSION = (bw unlock --raw)   # PowerShell; then lock when done
dotenvx bitwarden up
dotenvx run -- python main.py
dotenvx set SOME_KEY "new-value"
```

PowerShell may block `.ps1` — use the commands above or `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\env-run.ps1`.
